Add a button size option to the window decoration

The decoration took the button side from the title bar height, so a larger
button needed a larger caption font or a larger TitleBarPad value. Breeze
offers a button size option, and this commit adds the same option.

The ButtonSize key in the General group of kwinqtcurverc takes the five names
of kcm_breezedecoration, and an absent or unknown value gives ButtonDefault.
Each size takes the Breeze multiple of the KDecoration3 grid unit: 1, 1.5, 2,
2.5 or 3.5 units. The decoration rounds the side to an odd number of pixels,
so a glyph keeps a centre pixel. It holds every side at 11 pixels or more,
where the glyph strokes stay 2 pixels wide. The title bar grows when a button
needs more room than the caption, and TitleBarPad grows the title bar alone.
At DejaVu Sans 10 pt with no pad the Normal button goes from 15 to 21 pixels.

The glyph side rounds up to the next odd number, so Tiny and Small draw
distinct line art wherever their button sides differ. The context help mark
takes a round join at the four smallest sides, where its corner spike reached
the frame ring.

The settings module gains a "Button size:" box on the General tab, and a save
reloads KWin at once. The help text of "Titlebar text padding:" now states
that the pad changes the title bar alone. Out of scope: a per button size, the
window icon size and the title alignment option of Breeze.

The change sits on the branch work/kdecoration3 of the local tree, as the third
commit. The fork wyn/qtcurve holds that branch. Merge request !9 on
system/qtcurve holds that branch.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

